# Random modules whose predicates have random argument types and modes,
# and one to three clauses that are mode-correct for their first mode,
# with unifications, calls, disjunctions, if-then-elses, negations,
# higher-order terms and calls, modes with an inst variable, type
# conversions and unique lists clobbered by a call, shuffled so that mode
# analysis has to schedule them; some clauses are
# mutated into mode errors (generate-mode-programs.py). merkc must report
# mode errors on the lines mmc does.
#
# REQUIRES: mmc
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir %t
# RUN: %python %S/../../../utils/type-oracle/generate-mode-programs.py --seed 1 --count 40 %t
# RUN: %compare-types --modes --error-lines %t/*.m
